.TH MSG\-VERIFY 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.4.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
msg\-verify \- check a message signature against an address. No keys are read
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
msg\-verify \-\-address ADDR (\-\-message TEXT | \-\-message\-file FILE) [\-\-hex] \-\-sig SIG [\-\-chain eth|btc|tron|sol|cosmos] [\-\-format raw|offchain\-v0] [\-\-pubkey B64]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
.RS 2
  msg\-verify \-\-address ADDR (\-\-message TEXT | \-\-message\-file FILE) [\-\-hex] \-\-sig SIG [\-\-chain eth|btc|tron|sol|cosmos]
             [\-\-format raw|offchain\-v0 (Solana, required)] [\-\-pubkey B64 (Cosmos, required)]
.RE
.fi
The chain is detected from the address (\-\-chain, if given, must agree):
.IP \(bu 2
0x + 40 hex: Ethereum EIP\-191 personal_sign, SIG 65 bytes hex, v = 27/28, 0/1 or 35 + 2*chain_id + rec.
.IP \(bu 2
base58 P2PKH starting with 1: Bitcoin Core signmessage, SIG base64 (header 27\-34).
.IP \(bu 2
base58check T... (0x41): Tron signMessageV2 (TIP\-191 style "\ex19TRON Signed Message:\en" + byte length),
SIG 65 bytes hex, v = 27/28.
.IP \(bu 2
base58 32\-byte ed25519 key: Solana, SIG base58 64 bytes; \-\-format is required: `raw` (the message bytes
as they are, wallet signMessage) or `offchain\-v0` (solana\-sdk / `solana sign\-offchain\-message` layout).
.IP \(bu 2
bech32 with a 20\-byte payload: Cosmos ADR\-036 (draft spec, Keplr signArbitrary), SIG base64 64 bytes,
\-\-pubkey (base64 33\-byte compressed key) required and must hash to the address.
.PP
Options that do not apply to the detected chain are refused, not ignored.
\-\-message\-file uses the file's exact bytes (no newline trimming); \-\-hex reads the message as hex bytes.
Refused: segwit/taproot addresses and BIP137 segwit headers (35\-42), BIP322, other chains' message
prefixes (ltc, doge, ...), EIP\-712 (use typed\-data\-verify), the Trust Wallet Core 85\-byte Solana
off\-chain layout, Ethermint\-style (eth_secp256k1) Cosmos keys.
Output: {"status":"ok"|"signer_mismatch","chain","address","recovered"?,"v"?,"format"?,"hrp"?}; exit 0 only on ok.
Vectors: crates/tx/tests/twc_message.rs (eth, btc) and crates/blocktools/tests/msg_chains.rs (tron, sol,
cosmos round\-trip only); provenance in docs/PROVENANCE\-msg.md.
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
\-\-address
\-\-chain
\-\-format
\-\-hex
\-\-message
\-\-message\-file
\-\-pubkey
\-\-sig
.fi
Each flag's meaning is in the SYNOPSIS usage line(s) above (taken from \-\-help).
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
Output: {"status":"ok"|"signer_mismatch","chain","address","recovered"?,"v"?,"format"?,"hrp"?}; exit 0 only on ok.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Measured on Linux by the EXAMPLES below (scripts/gen\-man.py runs them):
.TP
0
last status ok
.TP
1
last status signer_mismatch
.TP
2
last status bad_input
.PP
Not every tool uses the same code for bad input: some exit 1, others exit 2 (docs/FINDINGS.md D1\-14). Always read the last JSON status line. Status and failure codes: docs/REFUSALS.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ msg\-verify \-\-address 19cAJn4Ms8jodBBGtroBNNpCZiHAWGAq7X \-\-message "test signature" \-\-sig ILH5K7JQLaRGaKGXXH5mYM6FIIy9IWyY4JUPI+PHYY4WaupxUbg+zy0bhBCrDuehy9x4WidwjkRR1GSLnWvOXBo=
# exit 0, last status: ok
$ msg\-verify \-\-address 1HZwkjkeaoZfTSaJxDw6aKkxp45agDiEzN \-\-message "test signature" \-\-sig ILH5K7JQLaRGaKGXXH5mYM6FIIy9IWyY4JUPI+PHYY4WaupxUbg+zy0bhBCrDuehy9x4WidwjkRR1GSLnWvOXBo=
# exit 1, last status: signer_mismatch
$ msg\-verify \-\-address TWWb9EjUWai17YEVB7FR8hreupYJKG9sMR \-\-message "Hello World" \-\-sig bc0753c070cc55693097df11bc11e1a7c4bd5e1a40b9dc94c75568e59bcc9d6b50a7873ef25b469e494490a54de37327b4bc7fc825c81a377b555e34fb7261ba1c
# exit 0, last status: ok
$ msg\-verify \-\-address H3imdwa5VQMB5V6yBNyrWwPdSKs4k9Pcpsu4diogoAcg \-\-message "Hello world" \-\-format raw \-\-sig 2iBZ6zrQRKHcbD8NWmm552gU5vGvh1dk3XV4jxnyEdRKm8up8AeQk1GFr9pJokSmchw7i9gMtNyFBdDt8tBxM1cG
# exit 0, last status: ok
$ msg\-verify \-\-address H3imdwa5VQMB5V6yBNyrWwPdSKs4k9Pcpsu4diogoAcg \-\-message "Hello world" \-\-sig 2iBZ6zrQRKHcbD8NWmm552gU5vGvh1dk3XV4jxnyEdRKm8up8AeQk1GFr9pJokSmchw7i9gMtNyFBdDt8tBxM1cG
# exit 2, last status: bad_input
$ msg\-verify \-\-address bc1qpjult34k9spjfym8hss2jrwjgf0xjf40ze0pp8 \-\-message hi \-\-sig AA==
# exit 2, last status: bad_input
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
It may open hostile wallet files and handle secrets: run it sealed and offline (./blocktools run; sealed\-run allows it).
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
